# SoftwareTeam Chat Commands

When the user types these commands, invoke the matching MCP tool from `project_controller`:

| User command | MCP tool | Then follow |
|--------------|----------|-------------|
| `/init` | `init_project_tool` | If `needs_enrichment`: example pack or digest enrichment per init.mdc; else report scan only |
| `/update` | `update_memory_tool` | Report incremental sync from recent_changes.json |
| `/docs` | `sync_documents_tool` | Report doc catalog sync |
| `/architect` or `/mode Architect` | `set_mode_tool("Architect")` | architect.mdc rules |
| `/coder` or `/mode Coder` | `set_mode_tool("Coder")` | coder.mdc rules |
| `/reviewer` or `/mode Reviewer` | `set_mode_tool("Reviewer")` | reviewer.mdc rules |
| `/mode Init` | `set_mode_tool("Init")` | init.mdc rules |
| `/state` | `get_state` | Summarize current mode and memory |
| `/test` or `/tester` | `run_tests` | Only if tester enhancement enabled |
| `/pipeline <task>` | `run_pipeline` | Only if pipeline enhancement enabled |

After Coder edits a file, always call `record_change_tool` with file path, summary, and diff.

**Init enrichment MCP tools (first init only):**
- `get_init_context_tool` — compact digest for AI enrichment
- `apply_enrichment_patch_tool` — merge curated JSON + sync symbols
- `apply_example_pack_tool` — zero-token curated seeds when available
- `render_memory_docs_tool` — re-render docs from memory JSON

**Memory tracks (do not mix):**
- Code architecture → `memory/architecture.json`, `docs/architecture.md`
- Code modules → `memory/modules.json`, `docs/modules.md`
- Project docs catalog → `memory/documents.json`, `docs/documents.md` (use `/docs`, not `/init`)
- `docs/generated/` is never part of code memory

Read context from `SoftwareTeam/docs/` and `SoftwareTeam/memory/` — not full repo search unless user explicitly asks.
